From 6b5ceab5d2dadf520839767aa0935dff8c45e894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: catlinux <marc.catlinux@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:50:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep XML elements that are not recognised so a rewrite does
 not drop them

Meta, Group, Entry (history included) and the Root element silently ignored unknown children, so rewriting a
database dropped whatever newer KeePass or KeePassXC versions had added. They are now kept in a new
unknownElements field (unknownRootElements for the children of Root) and written back.
